From 1e24a5bcaf8b8a5841a40544a32a32cec561d93e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:42:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] A 1D LUT of the display in the settings: .cal
 offered, any gamut, kodi.log says what it holds

The file browser of the LUT for SDR and for HDR offers .cal next to
.cube, .3dl and .3dlut, and their help says that a 1D LUT is taken.

A 1D LUT alone mixes no primaries: it is a curve of each channel. The
check of an SDR LUT against the gamut of the SDR output (a .cube taken
to be made for the gamut of "SDR LUT made for") refused a .cal on an
output in BT.2020 or DCI-P3 for no reason; DISPLAY_LUT::Fits() now
takes perChannel, and a 1D LUT alone fits an SDR output of any gamut.
Its signal is still checked (a file that says it is of PQ is not
applied to SDR, nor one of SDR to HDR).

kodi.log says what a file holds: a 1D LUT of n points a channel, or a
3D table after a shaper of n points, and where a .cal says it was made
in the levels of video.
